  "goodToKnow": "Das Insolvenzverfahren is insolvency proceedings, opened by a court when a company or person can't pay its debts. A Insolvenzverwalter (administrator) takes control and tries to rescue or sell the business. Individuals can go through a Privatinsolvenz and be freed of debts after three years. The colloquial word for bankruptcy is die Pleite. The 2020 collapse of Wirecard was one of Germany's biggest cases. The plural is the same."
